ONNX conversion pinned by OpenCV
--------------------------------
opencv_extra's testdata/dnn/download_models.py on the 5.x line names
these files wechat_2021-01/detect.onnx and wechat_2021-01/sr.onnx and
checks SHA-1 of the raw bytes:

    detect.onnx   SHA-1 8dff596d81e6c223f188defc2616df1c83a406ae
    sr.onnx       SHA-1 854b183017c2303cc429bcaf598cc7fc18e076a6

The bytes were taken from the URL that script pins, the v1.1.0 release
of https://github.com/omrope79/opencv-test-models. That release is a
personal GitHub release, not an OpenCV or Tencent organization
release. Each file's ONNX producer field is "caffe" and its embedded
path is dnn-models/dnn/wechat_2021-01/<name>.onnx.

OpenCV 5 reads the files with cv::dnn::readNetFromONNX inside the
WeChatQRCode constructor. OpenCV 4 cannot. tests/ lock SHA-256 of
these exact bytes.
